  "name": "Asian American creative jazz (Asian Improv movement)",
  "family": "jazz",
  "lineage": "Movement of Asian American jazz musicians centred in the San Francisco Bay Area from the early 1980s, who joined post-bop and free jazz with Chinese and Japanese melodies and instruments and with themes of Asian American history and activism. The band United Front recorded for RPM in 1981, and pianist Jon Jang and saxophonist Francis Wong founded Asian Improv Records in 1987, whose catalogue includes pianist Glenn Horiuchi and bassist Mark Izu; drummer Anthony Brown led the Asian American Orchestra.",
  "recipe": "classic North American 1980-1983 asian american creative jazz, improv On Frame, avant branch. selmer mark vi canonical 1954 1974 jazz paris continuous-airflow legato saxophone, grand piano, double bass, dark bronze bell bronze drum kit, erhu, cowhide canonical Japanese keyaki zelkova canonical Japanese single hollowed trunk taiko drum. live tracking. large-diaphragm condenser, API 312 op-amp pre, API op-amp console, 1176 FET, API proportional-Q EQ. Studer 30ips tape plate reverb.",
